After the printf moves disk $n$ to C, move the $n-1$ disks from B to C using A: `move(n-1, B, A, C)`.
```c
void move(int n, char A, char B, char C)
{
    if (n > 0) {
        move(n-1, A, C, B);
        printf("Move disk %d from pole %c to pole %c\n", n, A, C);
        move(n-1, B, A, C);
    }
}
```

If mutex was 0, TEST-AND-SET returns 0 and atomically sets mutex = 1: the loop exits and the caller owns the lock. If mutex was 1 it returns 1 and the caller keeps spinning.\n\n```c
int mutex = 0;
void enter_cs() { while (TEST-AND-SET(&mutex)); }
void leave_cs() { mutex = 0; }
```

Declare `semaphore mutex = 1;`. Insert `P(mutex);` right after p1/c1 and `V(mutex);` right before p2/c2:

```c
semaphore mutex = 1;
/* producer */
p1: P(b_empty);
    P(mutex);
    put the item into buf[first];
    first = (first+1)%BUFFSIZE;
    V(mutex);
p2: V(b_full);
/* consumer */
c1: P(b_full);
    P(mutex);
    take the item from buf[last];
    last = (last+1)%BUFFSIZE;
    V(mutex);
c2: V(b_empty);
```
